course: dictionary
lesson: 4795
title: Humbly: doing things modestly
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Words ending in -ly often tell you how someone does something. «Humbly» tells you the way something is done. It comes from humble, so ask yourself: how would a modest person act? Quietly, and without showing off.
explain: «Toad wants to argue, but he catches sight of himself in the mirror, the rusty black bonnet perched over one eye, and goes upstairs quickly and humbly.» Toad has just seen how silly he looks, so he is not proud any more. Humbly here means in a modest, quiet way. He goes upstairs both quickly and humbly.
explain: Read the words around humbly to check its meaning. «Humbly ask» and «humbly apologise» are polite ways of asking or saying sorry. In church, people «pray humbly», with humble hearts. Swap in your meaning: if it still makes sense, you have found it.
fact: Humbly means in a modest way, without thinking you are better or more important than others.
fact: Humbly can also mean in a very polite, respectful way, especially when you ask for something or say sorry.
fact: «Humbly ask», «humbly apologise» and «humbly beg your pardon» are common phrases.
fact: Christians believe that in Jesus God «came humbly, close to poor and ordinary people».
fact: In prayers and hymns, people come to God humbly, with humble hearts.
exercise: «Toad goes upstairs quickly and humbly.» What is humbly describing? | How many stairs there are | *The way Toad goes upstairs | The mirror on the wall | The colour of the stairs
exercise: «We humbly pray.» What does humbly mean here? | Loudly and proudly | While standing on a chair | *With a modest, respectful heart | In a great hurry
exercise: «Winners who thank others humbly are admired.» Why are they admired? | *Because they show they are not better than anyone else | Because they never speak at all | Because they shout the loudest
test: Ali says, «I humbly apologise.» Which word tells you how Ali says sorry? | *Modestly and politely | Loudly | Angrily | Carelessly
test: Which sentence uses humbly to mean in a modest way, without showing off? | She shouted that she was the best player | She boasted about her goal to everyone | She pushed to the front of the line | *She thanked the team and said she had only been lucky
exam: «Christians believe God came humbly, close to poor and ordinary people.» What does humbly suggest about God? | *Modest, close and caring towards ordinary people | Angry and loud | Far away and grand | Rich and powerful
